      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks better and also consistent with `equals(...)` ✅\n\nSome last thoughts regarding `getPlanElementAction()` though: \n\n1. It ends up relying directly and indirectly on `line.getAction()` (indirectly via `isSkip()` and `isComment()`). `RebaseTodoLine::getAction` may change its return value mid-fly, since `action` is **not** `final`, which may leave dangling entries in the hash map in `TreeViewer`. Have you checked what would it take for that scenario to happen?\n\n2. It may `throw new IllegalStateException();` in the future, if the logic changes. Right now I see all possible values of `ElementAction` are covered but that method looks brittle, because of the `default`. It\u0027s just a nit and it doesn\u0027t have to be addressed right now if it\u0027s too complex, but changing the method so that it considers all cases in the `switch` and removing the `default` case would enforce correctness at compile time, which is much better than letting the exception be thrown at run-time.",
